 ### [Hash Grid Neural Fields](3855-hash-grid-neural-fields.md)
-Hash Grid Neural Fields define a continuous scene function $F_\Theta: \mathbb{R}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^k$ by mapping spatial coordinates to high-dimensional feature vectors using a cascade of learnable hash tables at different resolutions. They solve the **spectral bias** problem inherent in standard MLPs, which struggle to learn high-frequency details, by allowing the network to capture fine structures without massive parameter counts. Unlike dense voxel grids which scale poorly with resolution, HashGrid uses spatial hashing to map voxel coordinates to a compact embedding table, reducing computational operations by approximately 70% compared to direct large implicit network queries.
